IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lb74-nouns`
IMPORT `lb74-cross-references`

-- Row il-74. EXPECTED RED: four assertions that fail on purpose, each stating a comparison of dates that the printed values do not satisfy, under each of the two counting conventions of the 30 months.
-- R1: the last period printed for section 230B of the National Insurance Law (SH 2232 section 1: from 29.9.2009, 30 months) ends on or after the day SH 2350 was published (1.4.2012, the footer's issue date). The last day is 28.3.2012 or 29.3.2012 by computation, which is 4 or 3 days before 1.4.2012, so R1 is false under both conventions.
-- R2: the last period printed ends on or after the day section 18(a) of SH 2350 counts the commencement to (31.5.2012, computed from the printed 60 days; the page prints no calendar date). The last day is 63 or 64 days before it, so R2 is false under both conventions.
-- The count, four, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red). If a later instrument is read that prints a longer period for section 230B, the assertions that it changes turn green and the declared count must go down with it.

§ `Expected red`

-- R1, first convention: the start day is day 1 of the 30 months.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)
-- R1, second convention: the months are counted from the day after the start day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)
-- R2, first convention.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`)
-- R2, second convention.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`)
